<title>POLAND: NBP drains PLN 381 mln from Polish money market.</title>
<headline>NBP drains PLN 381 mln from Polish money market.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland drained 230.6 million zlotys from the market through a seven day reverse NBP-bill repurchase auction and 150.6 million through a 14-day operation, the NBP said.</p>
<p>All bids have been accepted.</p>
<p>The bank drained the market for 14 days at an unchanged maximum rate of 22.15 percent and for seven days also flat at 22.09 percent.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 2 653 9700</p>
